  "Scenes.Amilyscene.AmilyKidMeetingGo.AmilyBouncingEager": "[pg]Amily is almost bouncing beside you as you wait for your progeny to arrive, but luckily, it's not too excruciating, and you can soon hear the first of the various squeaks and calls that herald your children."
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.AmilyKidMeetingGo.AmilyEnjoysHerself": "[pg]You can tell that Amily is enjoying herself just as much, if not more than you. She's laughing, smiling, dancing, and shining in the center of her family, surrounded by the fruits of her labor. Watching her revel in the shared love sets a warm feeling deep in your chest, and you elect to just sit and watch her for a time."
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.AmilyKidMeetingGo.ChaosOnArrival": "[pg]When they properly reach you, it's complete chaos for a few minutes. A veritable army of your kids vies for your attention, and you're completely occupied by shaking proffered hands and accepting incoming hugs. It's hard not to step on any tails, but you manage well enough, and eventually, you're able to greet all of the present mice."
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.AmilyKidMeetingGo.CrowdEnergyFades": "[pg]After a few hours of cavorting and merrymaking, it's clear that the energy of the crowd is flagging. Several of the most senior mice start making preparations, corralling the younger ones and making sure everyone is accounted for."
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.AmilyKidMeetingGo.ElationIsInfectious": "Her elation is infectious, and you soon find yourself following along behind her, hand in hand, as she babbles about all of the things she wants to ask them and all of the things she's worried about. You're swept along right up until you see a small grey blob on the horizon, which grows slowly but steadily until you can start to make out individual mice in its mass."
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.AmilyKidMeetingGo.MiceSayGoodbye": "[pg]When everything's been said and done, the mice all line up and say goodbye to you individually. There's a medley of crying, jokes, and hugs, and one little mouse-girl even plants a warm kiss on your cheek. But eventually, they have to go. You wave them off as the merry band sets out back for their village. Amily stands beside you, trying to stay strong even as her lip waves a bit. It might be sad to see them go for now, but the thought that they're out there, not just living, but prospering, fills your heart with a warmth that will last long into the night."
