  "Scenes.Amilyscene.EncounterAmily.AsksHermaphrodite": "[say: Never mind,] she says after a moment. [say: You're a hermaphrodite, aren't you? Forget I mentioned it.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.EncounterAmily.AsksTimeToTalk": "[say: Ah... do you have the time to talk? There's something I want to get off my chest,] Amily nervously asks.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.EncounterAmily.AtLossForWords": "Amily stares at you, clearly at a loss for words, and then shakes her head in disbelief. She tries to give you a smile. [say: Well... us girls gotta stick together, right? If you look for a bottle of Succubus Milk--imps seem to carry it on occasion, though I don't know why--then you can drink it to get your vagina back. Also, I'd find an alchemist first, so he can remove the corruption from it.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.EncounterAmily.AttentionToMidriff": "She seems to be paying more attention to her gravid midriff than to you, and it's several long moments before she finally speaks. [say: These children will be born soon. I guess I owe you my thanks for being willing to father them.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.EncounterAmily.BornHereSpits": "[say: I was born here, I grew up here, and I would have gotten married and settled down here if it hadn't been for those demons.] She spits the word 'demons' with contempt. [say: After it was all over, I had nowhere else to go. So I stayed here. I've still got nowhere else to go, to be honest. I haven't found any other settlements of my own people, and I'd sooner die than give myself over to the demons. But it seems that if I'm ever going to see more of my people living free, I'm going to have to take the leading role...][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.EncounterAmily.BornHereSpitsAgain": "[say: I was born here, I grew up here, and I would have gotten married and settled down here if it hadn't been for those demons.] She spits the word 'demons' with contempt. [say: After it was all over, I had nowhere else to go. So I stayed here. I've still got nowhere else to go, to be honest. I haven't found any other settlements of my own people, and I'd sooner die than give myself over to the demons. But it seems that if I'm ever going to see more of my people living free, I'm going to have to take the leading role...][pg]"
