  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ExcuseHeadBackCamp": ", politely excuse yourself, and head back to your own camp. It sounds like she's doing better at keeping a steady supply of food and water going than you are. But if that's the case... why does she look so thin?[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ExcuseOnceOkay": ", then excuse yourself once you are certain she is okay.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ExcuseSitBackCamp": ", politely excuse yourself, and sit back down in camp. It sounds like she's doing better at keeping a steady supply of food and water going than you are. But if that's the case... why does she look so thin?[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ExcuseYourself": " and excuse yourself.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ExecuteImpsBehind": "[say: When imps would wander into the ruins, I'd execute them from behind,] she says in plain fashion. [say: I seldom found anything useful on them, but as I started leaving the heads around the perimeter, they wouldn't show up as often anymore.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ExplainHowWorks": "You ask her to explain how that works.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ExpressionTells": "Your expression probably tells the story, because Amily giggles slightly before adding. [say: It's not dangerous or anything like that! The queen and the handmaidens both have this cock-like appendage on their abdomens; the queen uses this to lay her eggs into the handmaidens, filling up their abdomens, while the handmaiden then lays a mixture of eggs and honey into a person's gut via their anus. The eggs kind of... well, they sit there, and then, when they're ready to hatch, they just... come out.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.FoolsButHappy": "She sighs softly. [say: We were fools... but we were so happy, can we be blamed for being fools? Life wasn't perfect, the hunters often had to hunt imps, but they never invaded our streets, and so we thought we were safe. We quarreled and made up, we laughed and loved and lived... It was such a wonderful time.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.FoughtOffRan": "[say: I fought it off and ran,] she insists, looking a little insulted, "
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.FullOfTaint": "[say: Full of taint, no question of that. Succubi give it to males who haven't become demons yet; makes them better able to produce cum, and pushes them towards demonhood.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.GiantBeesStrange": "[say: Giant Bees? They're a strange race,] Amily says. [say: They're not really corrupt, but at the same time, they act kind of like demons.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.GoblinsCorrupted": "[say: You may have seen goblins while you were exploring? Well, they're corrupted creatures, but their corruption stems from chemicals in their blood. I managed to... persuade... a Goblin to get me some samples of a distillation of that specific chemical. Once I am certain I am pregnant, I can take a vial to cause my pregnancy to advance really quickly, and for the children to grow to full maturity in one or two weeks, like a Goblin does.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.GoblinsShakesHead": "[say: Ah, goblins.] Amily says, shaking her head sadly. [say: Yet another race corrupted by the demons. Used to be that all they wanted was to experiment with potions and build machines. Now all they do is fuck... Weird thing is, they seem to actively want to get pregnant. I've heard that giving birth is like the biggest, most prolonged orgasm to them.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.GoneToKillImp": " you have little doubt that she's gone to find and kill an imp.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.HatchHundredsBees": "[say: Giant Bees hatch from each egg as hundreds of regular-looking little bees. And fertiles are involved in that--for some reason, the eggs need to incubate inside a living being to hatch in the first place.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.HeLovedMe": "[say: What?] she asks, clearly surprised. [say: No, he loved me, and I loved him, but he didn't have a lot of free time. I tried to take an interest in learning alchemy, it was a way to get closer to him, but it never really interested me that much.] She smiles, amused. [say: I was really more of a mommy's girl than a daddy's girl, I guess.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.HeadBackCamp": "Thanking her for her time, and the warning, you head back to your own camp.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.HeyHoldOnSecond": "[say: Hey, hold on a second,] Amily tells you. [say: You were worried, weren't you? Worried about me...? About the children?][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.HintOfWorry": "A hint of worry creeps into her expression, matching your own; but she remains resolute. [say: The first of our kids grew up so fast, and they seem to be doing OK out there without their parents to dote on them. The eldest are doing a great job caring for the young ones,] she answers.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.HorseEssence": "[say: That's a distillation of horse essence, I think.] Amily says. [say: I guess it would probably make you stronger and tougher... but horses aren't smart, and it might be too strong for a human to handle without changing them,] she warns you.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.HowAnyoneKnows": "You ask how anyone knows this much about them, if even meeting one is so dangerous. Amily scratches her head a bit and blushes, clearly a little embarrassed to not have a definitive answer for this one. [say: W-well... it's mostly just conjecture. Like I said, I'm only repeating what I've heard.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.HowSupposedWork": "You ask how that is supposed to work, given that she is very obviously not corrupt.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.HowSurviveVillage": "You ask her, hesitantly, how she managed to survive the destruction of her village, and how she's stayed alive ever since.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.HowWouldKnow": "You ask her how on earth she would know that all sand witches have four milk-filled breasts. She blushes deeply and fidgets, clearly embarrassed. Finally, she speaks up.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.HunterBestVillage": "[say: She was a hunter--one of the best in the village. Quick enough to run a deer to ground, quiet enough that it wouldn't know she was there until her knife was at its throat, skilled enough with a blowpipe to pin a fly to a tree from fifty paces without killing it,] Amily boasts. [say: I admired her--I adored her, I wanted to be just like her. I was always bugging her to teach me, and she worked hard to help me get good. Everyone always said I was going to be just like her.] She smiles... and then she looks sad. [say: If it wasn't for those skills, I mightn't have survived when the demons came.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.HypnoticThrumming": "[say: Well, they mainly use this hypnotic thrumming from their wings; but if you've got a strong, sharp mind you can shake it off. They aren't the kind to get violent; they will ask you to accept their eggs, if you resist their hypnosis, but they won't try to beat you into submission so they can lay their eggs. I wouldn't recommend fighting them; they're quick and pretty tough, thanks to that armor, and they've got this nasty venom that saps your strength and arouses you at the same time.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.InsistWantKnow": "You insist that, yes, you do want to know.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ItsAllRight": "Telling her that it's all right if she doesn't know that much, you get up"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.KeepThatInMind": "Promising you'll keep that in mind, you take your leave of Amily.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.KihaName": " Kiha"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.LaughsRunsAway": "Amily laughs. [say: Not really; me, I run if ever I see them. I'm not a stand-up fighter to begin with, but against those brutes? And it's not just their strength, either... I think they've got some kind of addictive chemical in their cum. The stink of their presence alone can make you feel turned on. There was this one that managed to corner me; it pulled out its huge horse-cock and started masturbating.] She shudders in disgust. [say: I narrowly missed getting sprayed, but the smell... it was intoxicating,] she admits, clearly embarrassed. [say: My legs nearly buckled from arousal--it was so tempting to just give in and let him fuck me.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.LeaveMeAloneSobs": "[say: I'll be alright,] she sobs. [say: But... please... leave me alone now? Please?][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.LifeInYourVillage": "[say: Well, what was life like in your village, huh?] she responds immediately. [say: If I gotta share something private like that, then the least you can do is reciprocate.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.LightAndPlayful": "Her tone is light and playful, you think she may only be teasing, but you decide that it is fair. And so you start to talk, telling her about your village; you describe the people, your friends, the places you liked to go. She sits and stares at you, clearly not expecting you to share that kind of information, but she looks quite appreciative, and she listens intently. Finally, when you finish, she gives a soft, sad smile, shakes her head, and then starts to speak.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.LightAndPlayfulAgain": "Her tone is light and playful, you think she may only be teasing, but you decide that it is fair. And so you talk to her, you tell her about your own family, your own childhood. She listens intently, laughing with you at the funny things you remember, and nodding with somber empathy at the sad things. Finally, when you finish, she gives a soft, sad smile, shakes her head, and then starts to speak.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.LostInDesert": "[say: I... kind of got lost in the desert once. A sand witch approached me and asks me if I'd let her cast a spell on me. When I refused, she attacked, trying to beat me down so she could cast it on me anyway.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.LuckySkinIntact": "[say: You were lucky to get away with your skin intact.] Amily tells you emphatically. [say: Minotaurs are dangerous brutes--they're one of the biggest, strongest and toughest beasts around. I don't dare go near the mountains, not with those beasts roaming around. Sometimes they carry around huge axes, but usually they make do with just their huge, knuckley fists.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.MakeSomethingOut": ". Maybe you could make something out of it...[sayend][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.MilkProducingSlave": "[say: How should I know? Make me into some kind of milk-producing slave?] Amily retorts fiercely, tail lashing in agitation. [say: I didn't give her a chance to use it. Three sleeping potion darts in her face, quicker than she could blink. I was annoyed, so I pulled off her robes to bind her limbs--I figured that'd slow her down long enough when she woke up that I'd be far away. Her breasts were full of milk--so full I could see it leaking out of each nipple.] She blushes intently, clearly embarrassed. [say: I... I hadn't had anything to eat or drink for ages, I was starving and thirsty and so I...][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.NeverKnewDragons": "[saystart]Dragonscale? I never knew dragons existed"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.NeverSeenFace": "[say: Well... I've never seen one face-to-face, but I've heard some other travelers tell stories about meeting corrupted kitsune. Nasty pieces of work, if any of it's true. Most kitsune are fairly innocuous, if a little irritating. Sometimes they can actually be pretty friendly, if you play along right. They seem to get off on making mischief, but it's more or less harmless--the worst that ever happens is you wind up getting lost in the woods or find some kind of treasure that turns out to be a box of rocks when you bring it home. The corrupted ones though... they cross a line. Their tricks are downright vindictive... and once they finish tormenting you, they'll suck the life right out of you without a moment's hesitation.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.NoEquipmentAlchemy": "[say: You know... I don't have the equipment needed to practice alchemy, but I do know a few things about it.] Amily says. [say: If you can bring me a potion or a reagent, I may be able to remember some of the things my father taught me.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.NoIdeaConfused": "[say: I... have no idea what that is,] she says, looking confused. [say: I guess it's... slimey? Concentrate of goo? I think it's got something to do with whatever's been polluting the lake, so I wouldn't rub it into your skin.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.NoSpecificNumber": "[say: Well, I don't exactly have a specific number of kids I want to deliver,] she explains. [say: The goblin only gave me five vials of that chemical; five pregnancies are all I'll get. Once I use them, and they're all grown big and strong, we can leave this area and find ourselves somewhere else to found a new village. In a place where the demons can't get us, we can work on expanding our numbers, bringing my people back to life as something other than just fucktoys.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.NoWeaponsArmed": "[say: We had no weapons--we hadn't been well armed even before, and who took spears and daggers to a festival? It was pandemonium--we scattered in all directions like brainless animals. The demons just had to pick us off. Some tried to fight, but they were quickly overwhelmed--beaten down by superior force. Some of us must have gone mad from the corruption boiling off of them, because they just gave up and let the demons have them. I... I saw this one boy, he couldn't have been more then a year or two older than me. I could only watch as he just opened his arms and looked up blissfully at this monster with a human woman's face, cat ears, six pairs of big, milk-seeping breasts and a horse's cock as long as she was tall. She grabbed him, and forcefed him that huge dick--rammed down his throat and he just swallowed it and swallowed it, looking delighted as she pushed him to the limit.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.NobodyAverageGirl": "[say: Who was I? Well... I was nobody, really. Just an average little girl, a face in the crowd. Daddy was an alchemist; he made a lot of his money in those days working to purify items that were tainted in some fashion, but his primary goal was trying to come up with a concoction that could actually help purify someone who had been tainted already. He thought that there might be something worth investigating in pure giant bee honey, but he never did succeed.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.NodSeeSimilar": "You nod, noting that you can see how that is similar to some of the demons you've come across.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.NoddingPolitely": "just nodding politely as you process the information."
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.NotGetOnFather": "You ask if she didn't get on with her father.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.NotStrongestBut": "[say: Physically, they're not the strongest, but they don't have to be--once they've got you caught in one of their illusions, you're pretty much under their power. Despite that, they don't seem to be particularly evil... at least, for the most part.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.NotUpsetConfused": "She looks not upset, like you feared, but confused. [say: I haven't explained that already?] she asks. [say: I ran. I ran as fast as I could for my house--I ran for my hunting knife and my blowpipes. And then, my parents ordered me to run into the wilderness and hide. I didn't want to go, but I obeyed. I just ran and ran all through the night, stopping only when I was exhausted--and even then, I crawled into a hollow at the roots of a tree to hide. I slept until hunger woke me, foraged for something to eat, and then I crept back to my village. I found it ruined, and I've lived here ever since.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.OfficialNameBees": "[say: Well... the Giant Bees you've probably seen? The official name for them is the fertile caste, but folks tend to just call them handmaidens,] Amily explains.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.PauseDelicately": "You pause for a few moments, trying to think of a way to phrase this delicately, then ask her how she plans on caring for her children.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.PauseDelicatelyAgain": "You pause for a few moments, trying to think of a way to phrase this delicately, then ask her how she thinks your children are doing.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.PausesAnotherFact": "She pauses for a moment, and then speaks up with another interesting fact in an attempt to save face. [say: They do seem to have a strange fascination with tentacle beasts, for some reason.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.PensiveNoMales": "She looks pensive. [say: Odd... I don't think they have any males left, but on very rare occasions I've seen these weird tiger-striped shark-girls... and they always had huge cocks and balls as well. But, whether female or herm, they seem to only care about fighting and fucking... and from the way I've seen them going at it, I don't think they see any difference between the two any more.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.PigtailTruffle": "[say: That's a pigtail truffle,] Amily says, [say: It might give you pig ears and even tail! It would make you plump and cute-looking!][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.PolitelyExcuse": ", and politely excuse yourself.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.PonderQuestion": "You think for a moment, wondering what to ask her. Then you shrug your shoulders and tell her that you'd like to know a little more about her, that you want to get to know her better.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.PonderQuestionAgain": "You think for a moment, wondering what to ask her. Then you shrug your shoulders and tell her that you'd like to know a little more about her, that you want to get to know her better.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.PonderQuestionFifth": "You think for a moment, wondering what to ask her. Then you shrug your shoulders and tell her that you'd like to know a little more about her, that you want to get to know her better.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.PonderQuestionFourth": "You think for a moment, wondering what to ask her. Then you shrug your shoulders and tell her that you'd like to know a little more about her, that you want to get to know her better.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.PonderQuestionSixth": "You think for a moment, wondering what to ask her. Then you shrug your shoulders and tell her that you'd like to know a little more about her, that you want to get to know her better.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.PonderQuestionThird": "You think for a moment, wondering what to ask her. Then you shrug your shoulders and tell her that you'd like to know a little more about her, that you want to get to know her better.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.PromiseBeCareful": "Thanking her for the advice, you promise you'll be more careful if you see them in the future"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ProudOfHerself": "She looks quite proud of herself for that. Feeling a bit disturbed by her ruthlessness, you thank her for the warning"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.PuzzledAmusedOffended": "She looks puzzled and not quite sure if she wants to be amused or offended. [say: I do have lots of food stockpiled--that's why I'm looking thinner than usual, in fact; I've been carefully saving up and preserving as much food as I can. Or did you think I was that bad a hunter and forager? I wouldn't have lasted all these years if I was,] she states. [say: Besides, I have a special potion I bartered from some goblins... within a week or two, any children I have will be grown enough to hunt and forage for themselves. Don't worry, I can handle looking after them.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.QuizzicalPress": "You give her a slightly quizzical look and then press her on the details.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.RackBrainsHerself": "You rack your brains for a few moments, then ask her to tell about herself, about who she was, before everything.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.RackBrainsVillage": "You rack your brains for a few moments, then ask her to tell you what life was like in her village, before everything.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ReassuredNotEntirely": "Feeling somewhat more reassured, but not entirely so, you get ready to leave.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.RegainsComposure": "and regains her composure.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.RespectPrivacy": "Wanting to respect her privacy, you place a hand on her shoulder and give her a squeeze, attempting to convey that you will always be ready to talk if she needs it."
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ReturnItemPocket": "Thanking her for her help, you return the item to your pocket"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.RobesAllWomen": "[say: Have you seen them under those robes? They're all women, they all have two pairs of breasts, and those breasts are always bloated huge with milk. My guess is that they've gone mad like those Fetish Cultists; they're not proper demons, but they're still sex-warped. Maybe they use milk to try and nourish seedlings or something,] the mouse-woman shrugs.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SandWitchesNote": "[say: Sand witches, eh? Funny, it seems the only pseudo-humans left in this area that aren't demons are magic-users... even though it was their usage of magic that turned the first demons into demons,] Amily notes. [say: Or so I heard, anyway,] she adds.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SandWitchesTrying": "You ask her if she knows what the Sand Witches are trying to do out there in the desert.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SaysKitsune": "[say: Kitsune,] she says matter-of-factly, nodding gently. [say: There's a race that's hard to categorize, if there ever was one.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SentencePeriod": "."
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SentencePeriodBreak": ".[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SentencePeriodBreakAgain": ".[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SentencePeriodBreakFourth": ".[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SentencePeriodBreakThird": ".[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SentencePeriodQuote": ".\""
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SetOffToCamp": " As you set off back to camp,"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ShakeHeadRefusal": "You shake your head in refusal"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ShareFewThings": "[say: Well, they don't seem to be demons, exactly, but they do share a few things in common with them. In spite of that, they somehow seem to have an amazing resistance to corruption. From the tales I've heard, they existed in their current form already for a long time before the demons arrived,] she explains. Seeing your perplexed expression, she continues. [say: They have extremely potent magic, and they draw their power from living things to sustain it. They can get it in lots of ways, but it seems like their favorite way is through sexual contact. They form a sort of... link, with their partner, I suppose, and absorb small amounts of their life energy.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SharkGirlsVillage": "[say: Shark-girls? Near as I can tell, they used to be a village of humans who lived right here on the lake... then the lake got polluted, and turned them all into... well, what they are now.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ShockedThenSad": "Amily looks shocked, and then sad. [say: I knew you would ask this, eventually,] she murmurs. Her gaze unfocuses itself, memories she evidently would rather not recall coming flooding back. [say: It was the evening of the annual autumn festival. We were all in the town square, celebrating the end of another year and our success in stockpiling food to see us through the winter. That was when they came... a horde of them, spilling over the walls, smashing through the gates. We had no sentries up... we had no forewarning. We didn't know they were there until the screaming started.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.ShrugsUnfamiliar": "She looks at it and shrugs, not really familiar with it.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SitBackInCamp": " As you sit back down in camp,"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SitBackOwnCamp": "Thanking her for her time, and the warning, you sit back down in your camp.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SlimeFromGel": "[say: A blob of slime from a green gel? Hmm...] she looks thoughtful. [say: I think I remember my dad once telling me you could make a really strong armor out of a special distillation of green oozes. I can't say for sure, and I wouldn't have the equipment even if I did remember.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SmallTearForm": "You see a small tear form in her eye and trickle down her cheek. Unable to say why, you reach out and wipe it away with your finger. She looks at you, startled"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SoManyHorrible": "[say: There were so many of them... so horrible. Imps by the dozens, the hundreds, succubi, incubi, creatures I can't even name. Twisted forms, all blurring into each other...][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SoManyYearsAgo": "[say: Life in the village, huh? It was so many years ago... and yet, I can remember it almost like it was yesterday. The demons had already been around for a few years by the time I remember--I think I was born maybe shortly after they first appeared, I haven't celebrated my Day of First Breath in so long I don't really know how old I am. We had walls to protect the village, and guards, but we never really believed that we would ever have to fight. We were a peaceful, quiet little village; we had nothing of real monetary worth, we thought we would be safe, that the demons would just ignore us. We fished in the lake, went swimming and sailed boats to amuse ourselves, we gathered fruits and nuts and berries and mushrooms from the forest, we hunted birds and small game for meat.][pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SomethingInPockets": "You remember that you have something in your pockets that might be of interest, and show it to Amily.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SorryPainfulMemories": "You tell her that you're sorry for bringing up such painful memories"
  "Scenes.Amilyscene.TalkWithCuntIMeanAmily.SpiderSilkTailor": "[say: Some spider silk? I think I remember someone who could take these and make them into armor or even comfortable robes.][pg]"
